From 390b2fdb6143ddb98d57c9303eb0b819c7457aa8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: M2 Gate Closure Audit <audit@local>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 17:37:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] fix(H3.1): correct clearance scale conversion in
 _collides

_collides compared shapely's scaled-coordinate distances directly against
config.CLEARANCE_EPS, which is expressed in unscaled problem units --
create_tree_polygon multiplies by config.SCALE_FACTOR (1e15), so the
comparison was off by that factor and the clearance margin was silently
inert (only the boolean has_overlap intersects/touches test was actually
gating feasibility).

Not caught by H3.1's own test, since H3.1 only needs a boolean feasible/
infeasible verdict and the overlap check alone already gated correctly.
Surfaced while building H3.2's continuous search objective, which needs a
real clearance *value*, not just a verdict -- see the following commit.

Fixed by reusing validation.clearance.min_pairwise_clearance, which already
performs the correct scale conversion, rather than reinventing it.

Confirmed inert-not-broken: pytest tests/property/test_lattice_feasibility.py
gives the identical result before and after this fix (5 passed, 27 skipped).
---
 src/tree_packing/geometry/lattice.py | 24 +++++++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

